coder › Done. Here's what I changed:

**New module `src/tokenize.ts`** — exports `tokenize(text): string[]`, extracted from `wordCount`'s exact behaviour: lower-cases, treats a word as a run of letters, digits and apostrophes, everything else as a separator, and drops empty words.

**`src/stats.ts`** — both `wordCount` and `topWords` now call `tokenize`. `wordCount`'s behaviour is unchanged (same regex, just moved), so its results are identical. `topWords` was fixed by the extraction: it now counts case-insensitively ('The' and 'the' now collapse to the same word) and returns the n most frequent `[word, count]` pairs, most frequent first, ties broken alphabetically — the tie-break was added since the extraction fixed case but not ordering.

**Tests** — added `src/tokenize.test.ts` (lower-casing, separators, no empty words) and extended `src/stats.test.ts` (case-insensitive counting, most-frequent-first, alphabetical tie-break).

